  "text": "318305 03/18/2026\nPage\n101 of\n190$0000010\n1$0.00RESOLUTN\nCreek\nThe following method should be used to install a native erosion control log:\nBACKFILLE\nCOMFACTSOL\nMaNG LOG\nA.\nCut a native log to length, allowing for some overlap past\neach of the supporting tree stumps. Flush trim the\nbranches.\nKFLOW\ntier\nSALDNM\nB. Dig a shallow trench, slightly wider and longer than\nthe log, on the uphill side of the tree stumps. Set the\nlog into trench and against the supporting tree\nstumps.\nC. Backfill and compact the excavated soil along uphill\nside of the log barrier.\nThe following method should be used to install a sandbag\nsediment barrier:\nA.\nPlace a row of sandbags from the top of the curb to at least 3' into the driveway.\nCurve the barrier so the ends point uphill.\nВ. Place a second layer of bags overlapping\nthe first. Press the bags tightly together to\neliminate any spaces between the bags.\nC.\nD.\nE.\n2.\nSPILLWAY_-\nPlace a third layer of bags on top leaving\na 6\" wide spill way near the center of the\nrow.\nRUNOFF\nROCK\nAPRON\nIf the driveway is unpaved, construct a rock apron below the downhill side of the\nspillway (see section on outlet protectors).\nAdd 1 or 2 more layers of bags, if necessary, to accommodate higher flow. If using\nmore than 3 layers, place a second row of bags behind the first for reinforcement.\nLeave a gap in the top layer as a spillway.\nMATERIALS:\n101",
